    ,                        !- Design Level {W}
    26.55;                   !- Watts per Zone Floor Area  Source: xlsx G7 = 26.55 W/m2 (x 37.67 m2 = 1000.14 W).

! ===========  INFILTRATION AND MECHANICAL VENTILATION  ===========
! Source for ZoneInfiltration:DesignFlowRate "Zone1 Infiltration": xlsx Sheet1 C39 Building air leakage level = 1.0 m3/h per m2 floor at 4 Pa.
ZoneInfiltration:DesignFlowRate,
    Zone1 Infiltration,      !- Name
    Zone1,                   !- Zone Name  Source: xlsx G2 Zone1.
    Always On,               !- Schedule Name  Required by EnergyPlus; continuous is a modelling choice.
    Flow/Area,               !- Design Flow Rate Calculation Method  Derived from xlsx C39 (unit m3/h per m2 floor).
    ,                        !- Design Flow Rate
    0.00027778;              !- Flow Rate per Floor Area {m3/s-m2}  Derived from xlsx C39: 1 m3/h/m2 / 3600 = 0.00027778 m3/s/m2; Kept: modelling choice (the flow at 4 Pa is used as the normal flow, constant).
! Source for ZoneVentilation:DesignFlowRate "Zone1 Mechanical Ventilation": xlsx Sheet1 C31 Mechanical vent, C32 supply 20 L/s, C33 exhaust 20 L/s, C34 no heat recovery, C35 no exhaust air recirculation, C36 no natural ventilation, C40 specified fan power 1.5 W/(L/s), C41 fan flow control factor 1.0 (no effect).
ZoneVentilation:DesignFlowRate,
    Zone1 Mechanical Ventilation, !- Name
    Zone1,                   !- Zone Name  Source: xlsx G2 Zone1.
    Always On,               !- Schedule Name  Required by EnergyPlus; continuous is a modelling choice.
    Flow/Zone,               !- Design Flow Rate Calculation Method  Derived from xlsx C32 (flow in L/s for the whole zone).  Source: xlsx C32 supply = C33 exhaust = 20 L/s = 0.02 m3/s.
    0.02,                    !- Design Flow Rate {m3/s}
    ,                        !- Flow Rate per Floor Area
    ,                        !- Flow Rate per Person
    ,                        !- Air Changes per Hour
    Balanced,                !- Ventilation Type  Derived from xlsx C32 = C33 (balanced), C34 no heat recovery.
    1050,                    !- Fan Pressure Rise {Pa}  Derived from xlsx C40 1.5 W/(L/s) = 1500 W/(m3/s) = pressure rise / total efficiency 0.7 -> 1050 Pa.
    0.7;                     !- Fan Total Efficiency  ASSUMED: 0.7 (the xlsx gives the specific fan power only).

! ===========  DOMESTIC HOT WATER  ===========
! Source for WaterHeater:Mixed "DHW Heater": xlsx Sheet1 G10 DHW 2.0 L/m2/month (x 37.67 m2 = 75.34 L/month), C45 all taps within 3 m of the heat generation, C46 DHW generation 'Heat Pump (1.4)', C67 DHW energy source Electricity. MISMATCH, not changed: a heat pump with COP 1.4 needs WaterHeater:HeatPump:PumpedCondenser; WaterHeater:Mixed caps the thermal efficiency at 1.0, so electric resistance (1.0) is used and the electricity is overstated by 1.4 on a very small load.
WaterHeater:Mixed,
    DHW Heater,              !- Name
    0.05,                    !- Tank Volume {m3}  ASSUMED: 0.05 m3 (not in the documents); Kept: with the EnergyPlus default volume the heater cycles on and off more than once per second (39,000 warnings).
    DHW Setpoint Sched,      !- Setpoint Temperature Schedule Name  Required by EnergyPlus.
    ,                        !- Deadband Temperature Difference {deltaC}
    ,                        !- Maximum Temperature Limit {C}
    ,                        !- Heater Control Type
    1500,                    !- Heater Maximum Capacity {W}  ASSUMED: 1500 W (not in the documents); Required so that the heater can be simulated without a plant loop.
    ,                        !- Heater Minimum Capacity {W}
    ,                        !- Heater Ignition Minimum Flow Rate
    ,                        !- Heater Ignition Delay
    Electricity,             !- Heater Fuel Type  Source: xlsx C67 Primary energy source for DHW = Electricity.
    1,                       !- Heater Thermal Efficiency  MISMATCH: xlsx C46 Heat Pump (1.4); EnergyPlus limit 1.0 for this object.
    ,                        !- Part Load Factor Curve Name
    ,                        !- Off Cycle Parasitic Fuel Consumption Rate
    ,                        !- Off Cycle Parasitic Fuel Type
    ,                        !- Off Cycle Parasitic Heat Fraction to Tank
    ,                        !- On Cycle Parasitic Fuel Consumption Rate
    ,                        !- On Cycle Parasitic Fuel Type
    ,                        !- On Cycle Parasitic Heat Fraction to Tank
    Zone,                    !- Ambient Temperature Indicator  Required by EnergyPlus; the heater stands in the zone (modelling choice).
    ,                        !- Ambient Temperature Schedule Name
    Zone1,                   !- Ambient Temperature Zone Name  Source: xlsx G2 Zone1.
    ,                        !- Ambient Temperature Outdoor Air Node Name
    ,                        !- Off Cycle Loss Coefficient to Ambient Temperature {W/K}
    ,                        !- Off Cycle Loss Fraction to Zone
    ,                        !- On Cycle Loss Coefficient to Ambient Temperature {W/K}
    ,                        !- On Cycle Loss Fraction to Zone
    2.8668e-08;              !- Peak Use Flow Rate {m3/s}  Derived from xlsx G10: 2 L/m2/month x 37.67 m2 = 75.34 L/month = 2.8668e-08 m3/s (30.42 days/month); Kept: modelling choice (constant draw).

! ===========  ENERGY SOURCES, COST AND EMISSIONS  ===========
! Source for FuelFactors "Electricity": xlsx Sheet1 C71 primary energy factor 2.5, D71 CO2 emission coefficient 400 g/kWh (= 111.1111 g/MJ); C66 / C67 / C68 energy sources are Electricity.
FuelFactors,
    Electricity,             !- Existing Fuel Resource Name
    2.5,                     !- Source Energy Factor {J/J}  Source: xlsx C71 = 2.5.
    ,                        !- Source Energy Schedule Name
    111.1111;                !- CO2 Emission Factor {g/MJ}  Derived from xlsx D71: 400 g/kWh / 3.6 = 111.1111 g/MJ.
! Source for FuelFactors "NaturalGas": xlsx Sheet1 C72 primary energy factor 1.1, D72 CO2 emission coefficient 200 g/kWh (= 55.5556 g/MJ).
FuelFactors,
